  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive Higher Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">While Education is a fundamental human right, one of Sustainable development goals and a powerful force for transforming the lives of refugees and host communities, refugee youth worldwide face significant barriers to accessing higher education.Current data showsthat only 7% of refugees globally have access to higher education leading to limited economic opportunities, higher rates of unemployment, and confinement in low-wage jobs. While many governments have acknowledged that access to education is transformative for refugees and integrating them into national education systems is the only way to ensure sustainability, the reality is that many refugee youth see higher education as a distant dream.

Our multimedia storytelling project seeks to expose the efforts and challenges ofmigrant/refugee youth, ages 18-35 to access higher education in Greece and Kenya. Our project consists of workshops, focus groups, documentary film production, Research and a public media campaign (photos, social media, ) that will serve as advocacy tools to improve higher educational access and opportunities for refugees/migrant youth in Africa/Kenya and Europe/Greece. This project will use a participatory action approach which will help the concerned youth to be actively and fully involved in the project and the outcomes will inform the policy to bring positive changes to this issue.</narrative>
  </description>
