  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Photofilm For Change CBO is a refugee youth led organization legally registered by the government of Kenya. The organization uses media (films/documentaries) as an advocacy medium to address different social issues affecting the refugee community in Kenya to pushfor policy change for refugees to live better lives and contribute to the host country&apos;s development. The organization identifies an issue affecting refugees, produces a film about it and uses the film produced as an advocacy tool.

Photofilm For Change CBO is a refugee youth led organization. It is represented by an executive director whose role is to act as the official spokesperson and representative for the organization, oversees programs implementation and fulfill all decisions from the managing team. All Decisions are made by a managing team of 5 youth who are heads of different departments in the organization which make decisions in the organization. The management team is helped by an independent advisory board with professional counsel only.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Photofilm For Change-CBO</narrative>
